	    quid       	"36BB2CD10255"
	    documentation 	
|Default Implementation of a multiplicative HalfGroup (G,*).
| * The Interface is separated out, 
| * because it is used to simulate multiple Inheritance by Delegation. 
| * 
| * Design Decisions:
| * This class does not extend Number, because not every Realization of a Group 
| * maps to numeric Values. (e.g. Functions, Matrices etc.)
| * Instead it presents the conversion Routines xxxxValue(Object arg)
| * to convert from Number Types.
| * 
| * Not all Methods are implemented as Defaults although that would be possible:
| * mulAt (*=) is not missing, but raises an Error when being called. 
| * This is for one thing to keep this Class abstract 
| * and for another to indicate the Methods that have in any case to be redefined.
| * 
| * This HalfGroup must be concrete, because it is used for delegation, 
| * instead of being used for inheritance!
| * 
| * Abstract Methods:
| * mulAt (*=)
| 
	    
	    stereotype 	"Delegator"
	    superclasses 	(list inheritance_relationship_list
		(object Inheritance_Relationship
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38070377"
		    supplier   	"Logical View::BaseCopy::absCopyAble"
		    quidu      	"36BB22B9029F"))
	    realized_interfaces 	(list realize_rel_list
		(object Realize_Relationship
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD3808017A"
		    supplier   	"Logical View::GroupM::HalfGroupM"
		    quidu      	"36BB2CD101B4"))
	    operations 	(list Operations
		(object Operation "absHalfGroupM"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38080365"
		    documentation 	
|This Constructor is only used in Initialize and Terminate of abstract Classes
|	 * and should normally be marked as 'protected' or 'friend',
|	 * but all these Routines are not within one Package.
|	 * It is needed for the Child Classes to call
|	 * and replace Self by the Child Object with it's overloaded Methods.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "self_"
			    type       	"HalfGroupM"))
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "mulAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38080379"
		    documentation 	
|Abstract Method, only implemented to make this Class concrete 
|	 * to be able to delegate to this. Throws the #AbstractMethodError'	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "arg"
			    type       	"Object"))
		    result     	"HalfGroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "mul"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38080397"
		    documentation 	
|Multiplication: *
|	 * A Standard Implementation. Can be overwritten by faster Implementations.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "arg"
			    type       	"Object"))
		    result     	"HalfGroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "sqr"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD380803AB"
		    documentation 	
|Square: x^2 == x*x
|	 * A Standard Implementation. Can be overwritten by faster Implementations.	 
		    
		    result     	"HalfGroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "sqrAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD380803B5"
		    documentation 	
|Square in Place: x*=x
|	 * A Standard Implementation. Can be overwritten by faster Implementations.	 
		    
		    result     	"HalfGroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "cbc"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD380803B6"
		    documentation 	
|Cubic: x^3 == (x^2)*=x
|	 * A Standard Implementation. Can be overwritten by faster Implementations.	 
		    
		    result     	"HalfGroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "cbcAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD380803BF"
		    documentation 	
|Cubic in Place: x*=x^2
|	 * A Standard Implementation. Can be overwritten by faster Implementations.	 
		    
		    result     	"HalfGroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "Pow2PowAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD380803C9"
		    documentation 	
|Raised by an Integer Power of 2 in Place: x^=(2^n)
|	 * Here implemented as a concatenated doubling.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "n"
			    type       	"int"))
		    result     	"HalfGroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "Pow2Pow"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD380803DD"
		    documentation 	
|Raised by an Integer Power of 2: x^(2^n)
|	 * Here implemented as a concatenated doubling.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "n"
			    type       	"int"))
		    result     	"HalfGroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "Pow"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38090009"
		    documentation 	
|Integer Power: x^n	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "n"
			    type       	"int"))
		    result     	"HalfGroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "PowAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD3809001D"
		    documentation 	
|Integer Power: x^=n
|	 * This Implementation is only valid for positive n > 0 !
|	 * You can implement a similar Algorithm for Multiplication.
|	 * This Algorithm uses the binary Representation of the integer n.
|	 * You could also write this with Prime Factors, but the Algorithm would be less
|	 * elegant and also slower, because this one uses only 2*lb n Multiplications.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "n"
			    type       	"int"))
		    result     	"HalfGroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "copyAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38090031"
		    documentation 	
|Complement to copyAt() and shallopCopyAt().
|	 * Does a 'deepCopy', to a certain Level
|	 * i.e. also inner Components are copied up to the Depth.
|	 * Returns the itself for further use. 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "arg"
			    type       	"Object")
			(object Parameter "Depth"
			    type       	"int"))
		    result     	"copyAble"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "newInstance"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD3809004F"
		    documentation 	
|Creates an uninitalized new Instance of it's class.
|	 * This can in VB also be achieved by 'CreateObjectFromInstance',
|	 * which may be slower.
|	 * When overriding, use newInstance on all Components.	 
		    
		    result     	"copyAble"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "fromStreamAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD38090059"
		    documentation 	
|Fills this Instance with the Contents read from the String.	 
		    
		    parameters 	(list Parameters
			(object Parameter "arg"
			    type       	"java.io.StreamTokenizer"))
		    result     	"copyAble"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "testIt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set
			(object Attribute
			    tool       	"Java"
			    name       	"Static"
			    value      	TRUE))
		    quid       	"37BD38090077"
		    documentation 	
|Method to test all Implementations in this class.
|	 * Must call testIt of the super Class.	 
		    
		    result     	"void"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0))
	    module     	"Component View::GroupM::absHalfGroupM"
	    quidu      	"36BB2CD10254"
	    language   	"Java")
	(object Class "GroupM"
	    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set
		(object Attribute
		    tool       	"Java"
		    name       	"GenerateFinalizer"
		    value      	FALSE)
		(object Attribute
		    tool       	"Java"
		    name       	"GenerateStaticInitializer"
		    value      	FALSE)
		(object Attribute
		    tool       	"Java"
		    name       	"GenerateInstanceInitializer"
		    value      	FALSE)
		(object Attribute
		    tool       	"Java"
		    name       	"GenerateDefaultConstructor"
		    value      	FALSE))
	    quid       	"36BB2CD102B9"
	    documentation 	
|Algebraic Group (M,*,/,1):
| * Set of Objects with inner Operations "*,/" on any two Objects
| * In a HalfGroup any two Objects can be "multiplied" or "divided".
| * These Operations are associative, i.e. (a*b)/c == a*(b/c)
| * 
| * Commutative Groups are Groups where the Operator Matrix for '*' is symmetric,
| * i.e. a*b=b*a.
| * C++ can implement non-commutative Groups,
| * because * is evaluated in strict order.
| * 
| * Defines the additional Operations which should be redefined
| * to exploit the final Definition of the Operands.
| * A Default Implementation is done in 'absGroupM'.
| * There are more effective ways to implement these functions,
| * depending on the implementing class. This is only the generic Solution.
| * 
| * Design Decisions:
| * This HalfGroupM must always be synchronous to HalfGroup!
| * Unfortunately you cannot use Operators as Variables in Templates,
| * in C++ you would use Macros for that.
| * 
| * The Interface has been separated from the Implementation in Java,
| * because it is used for multiple Inheritance.
| * 
| * It can be Proved, that :
| * ...there is only a single ONE Element.
| * This Element is neutral for both left and right * Operations.
| * ...there is only a single inverse Element for each Element.
| * This is the same Element for both left and right * Operations.
| 
	    
	    stereotype 	"Interface"
	    superclasses 	(list inheritance_relationship_list
		(object Inheritance_Relationship
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD380A00D2"
		    supplier   	"Logical View::GroupM::HalfGroupM"
		    quidu      	"36BB2CD101B4")
		(object Inheritance_Relationship
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD380A02BD"
		    supplier   	"Logical View::GroupM::intGroupM"
		    quidu      	"36BB2CD10146"))
	    operations 	(list Operations
		(object Operation "invAt"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set
			(object Attribute
			    tool       	"Java"
			    name       	"Abstract"
			    value      	TRUE))
		    quid       	"37BD380A02C7"
		    documentation 	
|Inversion in Place: 1/x	 
		    
		    result     	"GroupM"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "inv"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set
			(object Attribute
			    tool       	"Java"
			    name       	"Abstract"
			    value      	TRUE))
		    quid       	"37BD380A02D1"
		    documentation 	
|Inversion: 1/x	 
		    
